  "notes": "Logo is the header logo as served by the site, without a size parameter. No heroImage given: the home page hero (Pleasure+Divers+Magnetic+Island.jpg, 1441x1080) is already in the facts file and no clearly better wide photo was found. Videos: none. The site embeds no YouTube or Vimeo videos and links only to Facebook and Instagram, which were not opened, so the videos list is empty. Gallery draws on the home, about, dive sites, dive courses and Dive Magnetic Island pages and leads with wildlife and people diving. Left out on purpose: the Best of Queensland Experience 2024 award graphic, the SSI Dive Center, Green Fins and Submerged Nation badges, the wave and arrow icons, and the PD_logo graphic (all graphics with text or logos printed on them). Also left out as possibly not the shop's own: Diving+Yongala.jpg, Museum+of+Underwater+Art.jpg and Great+Barrier+Reef+Dive+Trips.jpg, which sit on pages about trips run by other operators, and the individual portraits of Haylie, Chad and Minki the shop dog (only the shared team photo is kept). The site shows no photo credits anywhere, so none was attributed to another business or photographer, but wildlife and scenery shots (turtle, pufferfish, batfish, Alma Bay, Overlooking Alma Bay, Coastline Magnetic Island) have no stated source, so a person should confirm they are the shop's own. The Specialty Courses page has one set of six photos for all eight specialties, several of them portrait phone photos (IMG_ file names); they are attached to every specialty trip that is not a night course and are not labelled, so check they fit. Night trips use the three photos from the Night Diving page. The Kids Scuba page has only two photos, shared by the four kids trips. Trips without their own photos (Divemaster Internship, pool session) reuse photos from the shop and pool pages. The importer measures every photo, so each candidate is listed rather than judged by eye. No bot check or captcha was met on the site; 24 pages were read."
}